#: ../../source/installation.rst:697
msgid "Shared caching tiers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:699
msgid ""
"Beyond memory and the local filesystem, PartCAD can keep its cache of "
"built geometry on a memcached server shared by a team or a CI fleet "
"(``cacheRemote``), and in an S3 bucket that outlives both (``cacheS3``). "
"Both clients are imported only when their tier is switched on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:704
msgid ""
"``cacheRemote`` needs nothing installed: its client (``aiomcache``) is an"
" ordinary dependency, so switching the tier on is all there is to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:707
msgid ""
"``cacheS3`` is an extra, because its client pulls in ``botocore``, which "
"is larger than the rest of PartCAD put together:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:714
msgid ""
"Enabling ``cacheS3`` without it reports an error naming the package to "
"install and leaves the remaining tiers working."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:721
msgid "Visual Studio Code extension"
msgstr "Расширение для Visual Studio Code"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:723
msgid ""
"For an editor you already have. To get the extension, the tools and an "
"editor in one download instead, see :ref:`the PartCAD IDE <partcad-ide>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:726
msgid ""
"Running ``/pc:setup`` from a terminal inside Visual Studio Code or "
"VSCodium installs this extension along with the command line tools. The "
"rest of this section is how to do it by hand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:729
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This extension is available through the VS Code marketplace. The "
"corresponding marketplace page is `here "
"<https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=PartCAD.partcad-"
"official>`_. Install it from the Extensions view, or by id from a "
"terminal:"
msgstr ""
"Это расширение доступно через маркетплейс VS Code. Соответствующая "
"страница маркетплейса находится `здесь "
"<https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=PartCAD.partcad-"
"official>`_."

#: ../../source/installation.rst:737
msgid ""
"Every `GitHub release <https://github.com/partcad/partcad/releases>`_ "
"also carries the packaged extension as ``partcad-<version>.vsix``, next "
"to the wheels and the bundles. Install it from the command line, or with "
"\"Install from VSIX...\" in the Extensions view:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:745
msgid ""
"Use it to pin a particular version, to install where the marketplace is "
"not reachable, or to try a release before the marketplace has it. One "
"package serves every platform: the extension is a JSON-RPC client with no"
" Python and nothing compiled in it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:751
msgid ""
"**VSCodium** installs it from `Open VSX <https://open-vsx.org/>`_, the "
"gallery VSCodium comes configured with and where PartCAD publishes the "
"extension for it. It is not pointed at the Visual Studio Marketplace, "
"whose terms restrict its use to Microsoft's own products. Search for "
"``PartCAD`` in the Extensions view, or run ``codium --install-extension "
"PartCAD.partcad-official``; the ``.vsix`` above works there too. The "
":ref:`PartCAD IDE <partcad-ide>` needs neither gallery -- it ships the "
"extension inside the application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:758
msgid "If you installed the extension before it moved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:760
msgid ""
"The extension used to be published as ``OpenVMP.partcad``. It is "
"``PartCAD.partcad-official`` now -- a different publisher, and a "
"different name because the marketplace does not let two publishers share "
"one extension name and ``partcad`` stays with the old entry. Either way "
"the marketplace treats the result as a separate extension rather than as "
"a rename."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:765
msgid ""
"There is nothing to do. The old entry still exists and now depends on the"
" new one, so it updates like any other extension and brings the extension"
" in its new home with it. Your settings, which live in your "
"``settings.json`` under the same ``partcad.*`` names, are untouched. You "
"can remove ``PartCAD (moved)`` from the Extensions view once it has done "
"its job."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:774
msgid "FreeCAD add-on"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:776
msgid ""
"The ``PartCAD`` workbench browses packages, parts and assemblies inside "
"FreeCAD and imports them into the open document. It lives in the "
"``cad/freecad`` directory of the repository; copy or link that directory "
"into FreeCAD's ``Mod`` folder as ``PartCAD`` and restart FreeCAD:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:785
msgid ""
"The ``Mod`` folder is ``~/Library/Preferences/FreeCAD/Mod/`` on macOS and"
" ``%APPDATA%\\FreeCAD\\Mod\\`` on Windows. No Python setup is needed: the"
" add-on drives the standalone ``partcad-json-rpc`` service, using an "
"existing standalone installation if there is one and offering to download"
" a bundle if there is not. See ``cad/freecad/README.md`` for what it does"
" and which environment variables it reads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:792
msgid "Public PartCAD repository"
msgstr "Публичный репозиторий PartCAD"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:794
msgid ""
"The public PartCAD repository is hosted at `GitHub "
"<https://github.com/partcad/partcad-index>`_. If necessary, PartCAD tools"
" are automatically retrieving the contents of this repository and all "
"other required repositories and packages. No manual action is needed to "
"`install` it."
msgstr ""
"Публичный репозиторий PartCAD размещён на `GitHub "
"<https://github.com/partcad/partcad-index>`_. При необходимости "
"инструменты PartCAD автоматически получают содержимое этого репозитория и"
" всех других требуемых репозиториев и пакетов. Никаких ручных действий "
"для его `установки` не требуется."

#: ../../source/installation.rst:798
msgid ""
"However, if you suspect that something is wrong with locally cached "
"files, use ``pc system status`` to investigate and to determine the "
"location of the cached files."
msgstr ""
"Однако, если вы подозреваете, что с локально закэшированными файлами "
"что-то не так, используйте ``pc system status``, чтобы разобраться и "
"определить расположение закэшированных файлов."

